          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"cofield-nikkis-touch-80d5409e184d\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":1,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.9,\"analysis\":\"“I love you” primarily avows the speaker’s loving emotional state. In context it also contributes to a relational appeal, giving weak performative support, but it does not clearly undertake a commitment. Nothing indicates that the words are a reflex-like expressive discharge rather than an emotionally significant avowal.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The surrounding wish to be together gives the declaration some courtship or commitment-invoking force, but the speaker explicitly avoids demanding an immediate decision, so substantial P force is uncertain.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"A directly represented spoken declaration, apparently part of a message to Nikki, as suggested by the request that she call the speaker back.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The declaration occurs between admissions of persistent thought and a stated desire to be with Nikki. The speaker acknowledges complications, postpones any demand for a decision, and asks for a return call. This frames “I love you” chiefly as an avowal intended to disclose feelings and support a cautious relational appeal, not as a reflexive outburst or definite undertaking.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“I can’t stop thinking about you, Nikki. I love you.”\",\"supports\":\"The declaration is presented as an avowal of an ongoing emotional state, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“I know it’s complicated, but I want to be with you.”\",\"supports\":\"The avowal is embedded in a relational appeal, supplying limited support for P while not itself stating a firm commitment.\",\"confidence\":0.93},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“I’m not asking you to make a decision now, but please, just… call me back.”\",\"supports\":\"The speaker seeks renewed contact while withholding an immediate relational demand; this limits P and suggests a recorded or otherwise unanswered message.\",\"confidence\":0.9},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The passage provides no description of blurting, involuntary speech, or words functioning as affective discharge.\",\"supports\":\"Supports E=0: emotional significance and the ellipsis elsewhere do not independently establish expressive/reflexive core force.\",\"confidence\":0.9}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the principal avowal, with low P representing its limited role in a relational bid. Delivery and surrounding emotional pressure require no independent E or O classification.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
